/2","section":3,"section_title":"Exact Gaussian projection","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:c794b7ddbbcdea88647c445078d07cb439f25f45999a3db65fac92b0bb1e976d","file":"preprints/Memory-and-precision-in-noiseless-Gaussian-regression-September-27-2026/build/sections/projection.tex","line":37,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"578f6addb6998b51a8be1a4240ab8d7ecd21efb19f26a240a50a40d9b996f353","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Memory-and-precision-in-noiseless-Gaussian-regression-September-27-2026/build/sections/projection.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:c794b7ddbbcdea88647c445078d07cb439f25f45999a3db65fac92b0bb1e976d","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Memory-and-precision-in-noiseless-Gaussian-regression-September-27-2026/build/sections/projection.tex#L37"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{h:dv:finite-density}\nLet \\(d,m\\ge1\\) and \\(p\\ge2\\) be integers, and let\n\\(\\beta>m+p-2\\), \\(H,R>0\\), and \\(z\\in\\mathbb R^d\\).\nSuppose that \\(\\mu\\) is a finite nonnegative Borel measure supported\non \\(B(z,R)\\) and satisfying\n\\begin{equation}\\label{h:dv:ambient-bound}\n \\mu(B(x,r))\\le Hr^\\beta\n \\qquad(x\\in\\mathbb R^d,\\ r>0).\n\\end{equation}\nFor \\(0\\le j\\le p-2\\), put\n\\[\n J_j=1+3^j2^\\beta\\frac{m}{\\beta-j-m},\n\\]\nand define\n\\begin{equation}\\label{h:dv:moment-scale}\n \\mathcal B=(2\\pi)^{-m(p-1)/(2p)}\n H R^{\\beta-m(1-1/p)}\n \\left(\\prod_{j=0}^{p-2}J_j\\right)^{1/p}.\n\\end{equation}\nThen \\(\\eta_\\mu\\) has a nonnegative jointly Borel density \\(F\\)\nwith respect to \\(\\lambda_m\\), which can be chosen to vanish\noutside \\(\\mathcal E_{z,R}\\), and\n\\begin{equation}\\label{h:dv:finite-density-bound}\n \\|F\\|_{L^p(\\lambda_m)}\\le\\mathcal B.\n\\end{equation}"}
